@page "/settings"
@attribute [Authorize]
@rendermode InteractiveServer
@inject InventoryStore Store
<PageTitle>Configuration · GJNET</PageTitle>
<div class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">MAKE IT YOURS</p><h1>Map your network.</h1><p class="muted">Private configuration lives in the data volume, outside the code repository.</p></div>
<div class="panel"><h2>Inventory & connections</h2><p>Edit the JSON below to add devices, guest subnet rules, API connections, and scan targets. Save validates the entire document before replacing it. API credentials are referenced by environment-variable name.</p><p>Guest rules use the most specific matching IPv4 subnet; ties follow document order. Only explicitly listed shortcuts are public. Guest pages never show shortcut notes.</p><label for="config">Private inventory configuration</label><textarea id="config" class="config" @bind="json" @bind:event="oninput" spellcheck="false"></textarea><button class="button" @onclick="Save">Save configuration →</button><p class="notice" role="status">@message</p></div>
<div class="panel"><h2>Connection types</h2><dl><dt>proxmox</dt><dd>Cluster URL, token value user@@realm!token=secret in a host environment variable.</dd><dt>docker</dt><dd>Dockhand URL and bearer token variable. Reads each environment, including Hawser hosts. hostAddress optionally overrides the host for published-port links.</dd><dt>redfish</dt><dd>iDRAC URL, username, and password variable. Self-signed certificates are accepted by default. Set validateTlsCertificate to true on an integration to require a trusted, valid certificate.</dd><dt>devices</dt><dd>Any named host, address, ports, kind, and notes. Reachability uses ICMP and configured TCP ports.</dd><dt>scanSubnets</dt><dd>Explicit IPv4 CIDRs, /24 or smaller. ICMP discovery only; devices that block ping may not appear.</dd></dl><p>See the repository's examples/inventory.example.json for a complete configuration. Add a shortcut first to get an ID for a guest-page rule.</p></div>
@code { string json="",message=""; protected override void OnInitialized()=>json=JsonSerializer.Serialize(Store.Read(),InventoryStore.Json); void Save() { try { Store.Save(JsonSerializer.Deserialize<Settings>(json,InventoryStore.Json) ?? throw new ArgumentException("Configuration is empty.")); message="Saved. The next poll uses this configuration."; } catch(Exception e) when(e is JsonException or ArgumentException or NullReferenceException) {message="Configuration rejected: "+e.Message;} } }
<div class="panel"><h2>Automatic service discovery</h2><p>Enabled by default. Container ports and saved shortcuts are checked every poll. A broader web-port sweep of known VM and Docker host addresses runs every five minutes. Only HTML interfaces, login pages, and HTTP redirects become automatic dashboards; plain APIs stay in inventory.</p><p>Use <code>discovery.enabled</code> to pause discovery, <code>discovery.scanIntervalSeconds</code> (minimum 60) to change the sweep interval, and <code>discovery.vmPorts</code> to choose up to 64 ports. For VMs without working guest network information, <code>discovery.vmHosts</code> maps a source ID such as <code>cluster:qemu/101</code> to an array of host addresses. Source IDs appear in MCP inventory.</p><p>New services stay private. Pin discovered interfaces to shortcuts for custom names and sections, or hide ones you do not need. Manual URL edits replace automatic address tracking. Discovery uses read-only HTTP GETs and never starts stopped services.</p></div>
